                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "eba1941d-d793-37d9-98bc-f3354d09abbd",
                        "entry_id": "38c7c947-d35a-3681-aa27-5018e28cb776",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To hedge about; surround with or as with a hedge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9aa7b6a2-c467-422f-b9b3-1c00bf043170",
                                "sense_id": "eba1941d-d793-37d9-98bc-f3354d09abbd",
                                "text": "[...] so that, though he had neither fixed flag not fixed father to cloud his thought and behedge his landscape, he could still, he used to say, share in the gush about ancestry."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5368e41a-7723-365b-8926-d64d4bad7ccb",
                        "entry_id": "38c7c947-d35a-3681-aa27-5018e28cb776",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To determine the boundary or limit of; define."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dbad86c2-a867-429c-a9d9-bf1b49ef9bc4",
                                "sense_id": "5368e41a-7723-365b-8926-d64d4bad7ccb",
                                "text": "Having been spawned in a royal bed — perchance the same in which his great gran'dame Catherine was wont to receive her paramours — he becomes the most powerful of princes — haloed with \"that divinity which doth behedge a king\" — and all [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "56714a98-d0e8-3247-b799-d2f45b1e6210",
                        "entry_id": "38c7c947-d35a-3681-aa27-5018e28cb776",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To surround; beset; plague; hinder."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ff23d1be-5e8e-46e5-a226-1f812f30e229",
                                "sense_id": "56714a98-d0e8-3247-b799-d2f45b1e6210",
                                "text": "Reflection finds the circumstance unfortunate that most of the agreeable actions of life are either forbidden or else deplorably behedged with restrictions."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "413e88f7-57fa-4de0-adf6-18b0777f4db8",
                                "sense_id": "56714a98-d0e8-3247-b799-d2f45b1e6210",
                                "text": "[...] nor is it necessary to do more than call attention to a few indisputable facts to prove that the public policy he recommends would do little or nothing to ameliorate the hard conditions that behedge the toiling millions."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ff3182ea-9c5c-390a-a862-fc27d8cb26b8",
                        "entry_id": "38c7c947-d35a-3681-aa27-5018e28cb776",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To straiten; restrict; constrain; limit."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f30e9d21-bcee-4800-9fe1-705e55297df3",
                                "sense_id": "ff3182ea-9c5c-390a-a862-fc27d8cb26b8",
                                "text": "The remaining heirs are therefore not to be defeated by any of the restrictions that behedge the remedies available to the third-party beneficiary of a contract; [...]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
